    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42361" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salmăcĭdus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		contr. from salgama, salma, and acidus, of water, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>having a salt and sour
				taste</i>, <i>salso-acid</i>: salmacidum <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλμυρόν,</span> salmacidus <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλμυρός, ἁλώδης,</span> Gloss. Philox.
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquae (with nitrosae),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					31, 3, 22, § 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aqua (opp. dulcis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. Val. 5, 41 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fluvii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					4, 10, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
